-- An imported contract that reads a section GIVEN WITH NO DEFAULT, as an operand
-- (smucclaw/l4-ide#1118).
--
-- `unset leg` comes from ok/section-given-import-contract-def.l4, where `gate`
-- has no TYPICALLY, so nothing can say which branch the contract takes. Every
-- evaluation here stops, and the message is the one a single file gives: the
-- evaluation "needed to know the value of gate, but it is an assumed term". As
-- an operand of RAND or ROR it used to stop with an internal error instead,
-- which tells the reader to report a bug in L4 for a program that is only
-- missing an input.

IMPORT `section-given-import-contract-def`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`the leg` MEANS `unset leg`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`left` MEANS `unset leg` RAND (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`right` MEANS (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10) ROR `unset leg`

#TRACE `the leg` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `left` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `right` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30
